{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[],"authorship_tag":"ABX9TyMmQ4PkgJjLrqT/kEDyItM8"},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Algorithm"],"metadata":{"id":"-kH5trAqgH8k"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Algorithm** is a finite, step-by-step procedure used to solve a problem or perform a task in programming. It describes the logic of a solution before writing actual code."],"metadata":{"id":"o3FSSYoWgXsf"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["![image.png](data:image/png;base64,)"],"metadata":{"id":"E3XrYgOoiAdU"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Characteristics of an Algorithm\n","\n","-  Input: Data given to the algorithm\n","\n","-  Output: Result produced after processing\n","\n","-  Definiteness: Each step is clear and unambiguous\n","\n","- Finiteness: Ends after a limited number of steps\n","\n","- Effectiveness: Steps are simple and executable"],"metadata":{"id":"Unns-rmbg5Tg"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Why Algorithms Are Important\n","\n","- Help plan logic before coding\n","\n","-  Make programs easier to understand and debug\n","\n","-  Improve efficiency (time and memory usage)\n","\n","-  Allow the same logic to be implemented in any language\n"],"metadata":{"id":"SB2Rr1h3hNg1"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Problems on Algorithm"],"metadata":{"id":"bnv8rjZeinXY"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 1️⃣ Algorithm to Find Whether a Number is Even or Odd"],"metadata":{"id":"BOYkOsMMio8I"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Step 1: Start\n","\n","Step 2: Read the number N\n","\n","Step 3: Check if N % 2 == 0\n","\n","Step 4: If true, display Even, else\n","display Odd\n","\n","Step 5: Stop"],"metadata":{"id":"s-2Wu3fgj1pL"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 2️⃣ Find the Largest of Two Numbers"],"metadata":{"id":"5rHhnXF7kND5"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Step 1: Start\n","\n","Step 2: Read two numbers A and B\n","\n","Step 3: If A > B, display A is largest\n","\n","Step 4: Else, display B is largest\n","\n","Step 5: Stop"],"metadata":{"id":"iFzFCAndkC2m"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 3️⃣ Find the Smallest of Three Numbers\n","\n","Step 1: Start\n","\n","Step 2: Read three numbers A, B, and C\n","\n","Step 3: If A <= B and A <= C, display A is smallest\n","\n","Step 4: Else if B <= A and B <= C, display B is smallest\n","\n","Step 5: Else, display C is smallest\n","\n","Step 6: Stop\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"JgNqJ0GDkpHb"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 4️⃣ Calculate the Area of a Circle\n","\n","Step 1: Start\n","\n","Step 2: Read the radius R\n","\n","Step 3: Calculate Area = π × R × R\n","\n","Step 4: Display the area\n","\n","Step 5: Stop\n"],"metadata":{"id":"ID6KHC-Xkuee"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","#### 5️⃣ Swap Two Numbers\n","\n","Step 1: Start\n","\n","Step 2: Read two numbers A and B\n","\n","Step 3: Store A in Temp\n","\n","Step 4: Assign B to A\n","\n","Step 5: Assign Temp to B\n","\n","Step 6: Display swapped values\n","\n","Step 7: Stop\n"],"metadata":{"id":"YJIyXTs3ky65"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 6️⃣ Check Whether a Person is Eligible to Vote\n","\n","Step 1: Start\n","\n","Step 2: Read age Age\n","\n","Step 3: Check if Age >= 18\n","\n","Step 4: If true, display Eligible to vote\n","\n","Step 5: Else, display Not eligible to vote\n","\n","Step 6: Stop"],"metadata":{"id":"qVCvOQfBlLuZ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 7️⃣ Find Whether a Number is Positive, Negative, or Zero\n","\n","Step 1: Start\n","\n","Step 2: Read number N\n","\n","Step 3: Check if N > 0\n","\n","Step 4: If true, display Positive\n","\n","Step 5: Else if N < 0, display Negative\n","\n","Step 6: Else, display Zero\n","\n","Step 7: Stop"],"metadata":{"id":"_4aDoEvWlRM3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 8️⃣ Convert Celsius to Fahrenheit\n","\n","Step 1: Start\n","\n","Step 2: Read temperature in Celsius\n","\n","Step 3: Calculate F = (C × 9 / 5) + 32\n","\n","Step 4: Display temperature in Fahrenheit\n","\n","Step 5: Stop"],"metadata":{"id":"ike7oFfmlTLF"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 9️⃣ Add Two Numbers\n","\n","Step 1: Start\n","\n","Step 2: Read two numbers A and B\n","\n","Step 3: Calculate Sum = A + B\n","\n","Step 4: Display the sum\n","\n","Step 5: Stop"],"metadata":{"id":"UP9m0qlSlU6V"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 🔟 Find the Square of a Number\n","\n","Step 1: Start\n","\n","Step 2: Read number N\n","\n","Step 3: Calculate Square = N × N\n","\n","Step 4: Display the square\n","\n","Step 5: Stop"],"metadata":{"id":"pCU4OHPQlWzC"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Pseudocode\n","\n","**Pseudocode** is an informal, human-readable description of a program’s logic written in simple English mixed with programming-like statements. It helps programmers plan and understand a solution before writing actual code.\n","\n","-  Its like Code in English\n","-  Its not a Programming Launguge no {} ; no syntax required\n","-  Focuses on logic, not on syntax\n","\n","\n","### Why Pseudocode Is Important\n","\n","- Helps design algorithms clearly\n","- Makes logic easy to explain and review\n","- Reduces coding errors\n","- Before wring real code ,we must be very clear about the steps.\n","Pseudocode helps us think,plan,and visualize the logic without\n","worrying about any language syntax\n"],"metadata":{"id":"bzWXERL4mcuc"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Problems on Pseudocode"],"metadata":{"id":"JhEPGfDvAGmK"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 1️⃣ Find Whether a Number is Even or Odd\n","\n","```\n","START\n","READ N\n","IF N MOD 2 = 0 THEN\n","    PRINT \"Even\"\n","ELSE\n","    PRINT \"Odd\"\n","END IF\n","STOP\n","```\n","\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"2veGYtq576cl"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 2️⃣ Find the Largest of Two Numbers\n","\n","```\n","START\n","READ A, B\n","IF A > B THEN\n","    PRINT A, \"is the largest\"\n","ELSE\n","    PRINT B, \"is the largest\"\n","END IF\n","STOP\n","```\n","\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"sOCm48yy9EPk"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","#### 3️⃣ Find the Smallest of Three Numbers\n","```\n","START\n","READ A, B, C\n","IF A <= B AND A <= C THEN\n","    PRINT A, \"is the small\"\n","ELSE IF B <= A AND B <= C THEN\n","    PRINT B, \"is the small\"\n","ELSE\n","    PRINT C, \"is the small\"\n","END IF\n","STOP\n","```\n"],"metadata":{"id":"Ju9Phd_B9KvX"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 4️⃣ Calculate the Area of a Circle\n","```\n","START\n","READ R\n","AREA = pie × R × R\n","PRINT AREA\n","STOP\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"k0NLrB1-9Um5"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","#### 5️⃣ Swap Two Numbers\n","```\n","START\n","READ A, B\n","TEMP = A\n","A = B\n","B = TEMP\n","PRINT A, B\n","STOP\n","```\n"],"metadata":{"id":"EcC2DGYC9k-d"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 6️⃣ Check Whether a Person is Eligible to Vote\n","```\n","START\n","READ Age\n","IF Age >= 18 THEN\n","    PRINT \"Eligible to vote\"\n","ELSE\n","    PRINT \"Not eligible to vote\"\n","END IF\n","STOP\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"kGO6NVIi9vpD"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 7️⃣ Find Whether a Number is Positive, Negative, or Zero\n","```\n","START\n","READ N\n","IF N > 0 THEN\n","    PRINT \"Positive\"\n","ELSE IF N < 0 THEN\n","    PRINT \"Negative\"\n","ELSE\n","    PRINT \"Zero\"\n","END IF\n","STOP\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"rulxPpql91EG"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","#### 8️⃣ Convert Celsius to Fahrenheit\n","```\n","START\n","READ C\n","F = (C × 9 / 5) + 32\n","PRINT F\n","STOP\n","\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"FZH2Bo-T979l"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 9️⃣ Add Two Numbers\n","```\n","START\n","READ A, B\n","SUM = A + B\n","PRINT SUM\n","STOP\n","\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"3fYNPVfj9_Nu"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 🔟 Find the Square of a Number\n","```\n","START\n","READ N\n","SQR = N × N\n","PRINT SQUARE\n","STOP\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"FfL9r-Eo-CKF"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### 1. sequential problem solving\n","```\n","no decisions, no loops, steps happen exactly in order\n","Example ADD 2NUMBERS\n","Input : AB\n","Output : sum of A and B\n","Start\n","Read input A\n","Read input B\n","Compute Sum= A+B\n","Display sum\n","Stop\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"y7wBBrIr_ZTo"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["![image.png](data:image/png;base64,)"],"metadata":{"id":"GKc7U--GDOfK"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["4. Decomposition (divide into smaller task)\n","```\n","Break large problem into small, managbJe sub problem\n","Example ATM withdrawal process:\n","Input: IN I\n","Output : Sum of numbers from 1 to N\n","Start\n","Read input N\n","Set sum\n","Set\n","Repeat while i<=n\n","-add I to sum\n","-increment I value\n","Stop\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"cnnP9IbxGVil"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# FLowcharts"],"metadata":{"id":"Es6NTkPdYyas"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","A flow chart is a visual representation of steps in an algorithm or\n","process\"\n","It uses symbols to show actions,decisions,inputs,and outputs in a\n","clear and logical flow\n","1"],"metadata":{"id":"943OuszBYvgG"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"l9dlB4qtDU9J"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"yh2gJj_Jd8bX"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# What is a time complexity ?\n"],"metadata":{"id":"U4IRoekXdpEb"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\"how long an algorithm takes to run based on the size of the input.\"\n","-  It does not measure time in seconds , because seconds can be change from ,Computer to computer ,internet speed, processor speed , Instead we can measure time complexity in number of operation\n","#### How do we measure ?\n","we use Big- O notation like:\n","-  0(1)-> constant time\n","-  O(n)\n"],"metadata":{"id":"7zbCaxJZduGJ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Sorting"],"metadata":{"id":"BI30A2VH33Wr"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Bubble sort\n","\n","- Bubble Sort is a simple comparison-based sorting algorithm.\n","\n","- It works by repeatedly comparing adjacent elements in a list.\n","\n","- If two adjacent elements are in the wrong order, they are swapped.\n","\n","- This process continues until no swaps are needed, meaning the list is sorted.\n","\n","- After each pass, the largest element “bubbles up” to its correct position at the end.\n","\n","```\n","Approach: Repeated swapping of adjacent elements\n","\n","Time Complexity:\n","Best Case: O(n) (already sorted)\n","Average Case: O(n²)\n","Worst Case: O(n²)\n","\n","Space Complexity: O(1) (in-place sorting)\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"l2-U1A_135u6"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Algorithm Steps (Bubble Sort)\n","\n","Step 1: Start\n","\n","Step 2: Read the number of elements n\n","\n","Step 3: Read the array elements\n","\n","Step 4: Repeat the following steps for i = 0 to n − 2\n","\n","Step 5: Compare adjacent elements arr[j] and arr[j + 1]\n","\n","Step 6: If arr[j] > arr[j + 1], swap them\n","\n","Step 7: Continue comparisons for j = 0 to n − i − 2\n","\n","Step 8: Repeat until the array is sorted\n","\n","Step 9: Display the sorted array\n","\n","Step 10: Stop"],"metadata":{"id":"471dFBy3pLaX"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Pseudocode (Bubble Sort)\n","\n","\n","\n","```BEGIN\n","  READ n\n","  READ array arr[0..n-1]\n","\n","  FOR i ← 0 TO n-2 DO\n","    FOR j ← 0 TO n-i-2 DO\n","      IF arr[j] > arr[j+1] THEN\n","        temp ← arr[j]\n","        arr[j] ← arr[j+1]\n","        arr[j+1] ← temp\n","      END IF\n","    END FOR\n","  END FOR\n","\n","  DISPLAY arr\n","END\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"7ZOZEKhRpAdq"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["arr = [5, 2, 9, 1, 3]\n","\n","n = len(arr)\n","for i in range(n):\n","    for j in range(0, n - i - 1):\n","        if arr[j] > arr[j + 1]:\n","            arr[j], arr[j + 1] = arr[j + 1], arr[j]\n","\n","print(\"Sorted array:\", arr)\n"],"metadata":{"id":"67bU1E8T39YC","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1768215797657,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":34,"user":{"displayName":"Dip Hire","userId":"01292357452111969469"}},"outputId":"4d921c3f-ffd2-4bf1-8332-7dbe1d96f951","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"}},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Sorted array: [1, 2, 3, 5, 9]\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Example Bubble sort\n"],"metadata":{"id":"pPVbMvFUu5RQ"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["Given Array: 32, 14, 27, 19, 42, 10, 4, 7\n","\n","Pass 1\n","Compare adjacent elements and swap if needed.\n","(32,14) → swap → 14, 32, 27, 19, 42, 10, 4, 7\n","(32,27) → swap → 14, 27, 32, 19, 42, 10, 4, 7\n","(32,19) → swap → 14, 27, 19, 32, 42, 10, 4, 7\n","(32,42) → no swap → 14, 27, 19, 32, 42, 10, 4, 7\n","(42,10) → swap → 14, 27, 19, 32, 10, 42, 4, 7\n","(42,4) → swap → 14, 27, 19, 32, 10, 4, 42, 7\n","(42,7) → swap → 14, 27, 19, 32, 10, 4, 7, 42\n","\n","# Largest element 42 fixed at the end.\n","\n","Pass 2\n","(14,27) → no swap\n","(27,19) → swap → 14, 19, 27, 32, 10, 4, 7, 42\n","(27,32) → no swap\n","(32,10) → swap → 14, 19, 27, 10, 32, 4, 7, 42\n","(32,4) → swap → 14, 19, 27, 10, 4, 32, 7, 42\n","(32,7) → swap → 14, 19, 27, 10, 4, 7, 32, 42\n","\n","32 fixed.\n","\n","Pass 3\n","(14,19) → no swap\n","(19,27) → no swap\n","(27,10) → swap → 14, 19, 10, 27, 4, 7, 32, 42\n","(27,4) → swap → 14, 19, 10, 4, 27, 7, 32, 42\n","(27,7) → swap → 14, 19, 10, 4, 7, 27, 32, 42\n","\n","27 fixed.\n","\n","Pass 4\n","(14,19) → no swap\n","(19,10) → swap → 14, 10, 19, 4, 7, 27, 32, 42\n","(19,4) → swap → 14, 10, 4, 19, 7, 27, 32, 42\n","(19,7) → swap → 14, 10, 4, 7, 19, 27, 32, 42\n","\n","19 fixed.\n","\n","Pass 5\n","\n","(14,10) → swap → 10, 14, 4, 7, 19, 27, 32, 42\n","(14,4) → swap → 10, 4, 14, 7, 19, 27, 32, 42\n","(14,7) → swap → 10, 4, 7, 14, 19, 27, 32, 42\n","\n","14 fixed.\n","\n","Pass 6\n","\n","(10,4) → swap → 4, 10, 7, 14, 19, 27, 32, 42\n","(10,7) → swap → 4, 7, 10, 14, 19, 27, 32, 42\n","\n","10 fixed.\n","\n","Pass 7\n","\n","(4,7) → no swap\n","\n","No swaps → array is sorted\n","\n","Final Sorted Array\n","\n","4, 7, 10, 14, 19, 27, 32, 42"],"metadata":{"id":"k3eCS0fd394M"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Insertion Sort"],"metadata":{"id":"D8fGn7fR_sgs"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Insertion Sort is a simple and intuitive sorting algorithm that works the way you sort playing cards in your hand.\n","\n","- Divide the array into sorted and unsorted parts.\n","- Take one element from the unsorted part.\n","- Insert it into its correct position in the sorted part.\n","- Repeat until the array is fully sorted.\n","\n","\n","\n","```\n","Time Complexity\n","Best Case: O(n) (already sorted)\n","Average Case: O(n²)\n","Worst Case: O(n²)\n","\n","Space Complexity\n","O(1) (in-place sorting)\n","```\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"VMDcDc5lowF7"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Algorithm Steps (Insertion Sort)\n"],"metadata":{"id":"Twrk99OUp2HW"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["Step 1: Start\n","Step 2: Read the number of elements n\n","Step 3: Read the array elements A[0] to A[n-1]\n","Step 4: Set i = 1\n","Step 5: Repeat steps 6 to 9 while i < n\n","Step 6: Set key = A[i]\n","Step 7: Set j = i - 1\n","Step 8: While j >= 0 and A[j] > key\n","        Move A[j] to A[j + 1]\n","        Decrease j by 1\n","Step 9: Insert key at position A[j + 1]\n","Step 10: Increment i by 1 and repeat\n","Step 11: Display the sorted array\n","Step 12: Stop"],"metadata":{"id":"ilXnOK1mpmUe"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","#### Pseudocode (Bubble Sort)\n","\n","```\n","InsertionSort(A, n)\n","    for i ← 1 to n - 1\n","        key ← A[i]\n","        j ← i - 1\n","\n","        while j ≥ 0 AND A[j] > key\n","            A[j + 1] ← A[j]\n","            j ← j - 1\n","        end while\n","\n","        A[j + 1] ← key\n","    end for\n","end\n","```\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"u6D_fTUbqDhB"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Example of Insertion sort\n","\n","```\n","Given Array:\n","32, 14, 27, 19, 42, 10, 4, 7\n","\n","Pass 1 (Insert 14)\n","Sorted part: 32\n","Compare 14 with 32 → shift 32\n","\n","14, 32, 27, 19, 42, 10, 4, 7\n","\n","Pass 2 (Insert 27)\n","Sorted part: 14, 32\n","27 < 32 → shift 32\n","27 > 14 → insert after 14\n","\n","14, 27, 32, 19, 42, 10, 4, 7\n","\n","Pass 3 (Insert 19)\n","Sorted part: 14, 27, 32\n","19 < 32 → shift\n","19 < 27 → shift\n","19 > 14 → insert\n","\n","14, 19, 27, 32, 42, 10, 4, 7\n","\n","Pass 4 (Insert 42)\n","Sorted part: 14, 19, 27, 32\n","42 > 32 → no shift\n","\n","14, 19, 27, 32, 42, 10, 4, 7\n","\n","Pass 5 (Insert 10)\n","Sorted part: 14, 19, 27, 32, 42\n","10 < 42 → shift\n","10 < 32 → shift\n","10 < 27 → shift\n","10 < 19 → shift\n","10 < 14 → shift\n","\n","Insert 10 at beginning\n","\n","10, 14, 19, 27, 32, 42, 4, 7\n","\n","Pass 6 (Insert 4)\n","Sorted part: 10, 14, 19, 27, 32, 42\n","4 is smaller than all → shift all\n","\n","4, 10, 14, 19, 27, 32, 42, 7\n","\n","Pass 7 (Insert 7)\n","Sorted part: 4, 10, 14, 19, 27, 32, 42\n","7 < 42 → shift\n","7 < 32 → shift\n","7 < 27 → shift\n","7 < 19 → shift\n","7 < 14 → shift\n","7 < 10 → shift\n","7 > 4 → insert\n","\n","4, 7, 10, 14, 19, 27, 32, 42\n","\n","Final Sorted Array\n","4, 7, 10, 14, 19, 27, 32, 42"],"metadata":{"id":"-qL08G0wqPXB"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Selection Sort"],"metadata":{"id":"YK4sYi-Oqvke"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","It repeatedly finds the minimum element from the unsorted part of the array and places it at the beginning.\n","\n","- Selection Sort is a simple comparison-based sorting algorithm.\n","\n","- The array is divided into two parts:\n","\n","   - Sorted part (left)\n","\n","   - Unsorted part (right)\n","\n","- Works well for small datasets, but inefficient for large data.\n","\n","\n","```\n","Time Complexity:\n","\n","Best Case: O(n²)\n","Average Case: O(n²)\n","Worst Case: O(n²)\n","\n","Space Complexity: O(1)\n","```\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"sqs-H-H4qvkg"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Algorithm Steps (Selection Sort)\n"],"metadata":{"id":"ph0NfGHiqvkh"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["Step 1: Start\n","Step 2: Read array size n\n","Step 3: For i = 0 to n-2\n","Step 4: Assume min_index = i\n","Step 5: For j = i+1 to n-1\n","Step 6: If array[j] < array[min_index], update min_index = j\n","Step 7: Swap array[i] and array[min_index]\n","Step 8: Repeat steps until array is sorted\n","Step 9: Stop"],"metadata":{"id":"Y5B7AhTpqvkh"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","#### Pseudocode (selection Sort)\n","\n","```\n","SelectionSort(A, n)\n","for i ← 0 to n-2 do\n","    min_index ← i\n","    for j ← i+1 to n-1 do\n","        if A[j] < A[min_index] then\n","            min_index ← j\n","    end for\n","    swap A[i] and A[min_index]\n","end for\n","\n","```\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"zglzIf5tqvki"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Example of Selection sort\n","\n","```\n","Given Array\n","[64, 25, 12, 22, 11]\n","\n","Pass 1 (i = 0)\n","Minimum element in unsorted part → 11\n","\n","Swap 64 and 11\n","\n","[11, 25, 12, 22, 64]\n","\n","Pass 2 (i = 1)\n","Minimum element in unsorted part → 12\n","\n","Swap 25 and 12\n","\n","[11, 12, 25, 22, 64]\n","\n","Pass 3 (i = 2)\n","Minimum element in unsorted part → 22\n","\n","Swap 25 and 22\n","\n","[11, 12, 22, 25, 64]\n","\n","Pass 4 (i = 3)\n","Minimum element in unsorted part → 25\n","\n","Swap 25 with itself (no change)\n","\n","[11, 12, 22, 25, 64]\n","\n","Final Sorted Array\n","[11, 12, 22, 25, 64]"],"metadata":{"id":"CSoP3zSRqvki"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Merge sort"],"metadata":{"id":"ycUKqtvsKDl-"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Merge Sort is a divide and conquer sorting algorithm.\n","It divides the array into smaller parts, sorts them recursively, and then merges the sorted parts.\n","\n","- Divide array into two halves\n","- Recursively sort each half\n","- Merge the sorted halves\n","- Stable sorting algorithm\n","- Works well for large datasets\n","\n","\n","```\n","Time Complexity:\n","Best Case: O(n log n)\n","Average Case: O(n log n)\n","Worst Case: O(n log n)\n","\n","Space Complexity: O(n)\n","```\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"E6tET5M4KDmA"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Algorithm Steps (Merge Sort)\n"],"metadata":{"id":"epdDjVi-KDmA"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["Start\n","If array size is greater than 1\n","Find the middle index\n","Divide array into left and right halves\n","Apply Merge Sort on left half\n","Apply Merge Sort on right half\n","Merge both sorted halves\n","Stop"],"metadata":{"id":"D8ZW1UEpKDmA"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","#### Pseudocode (selection Sort)\n","\n","```\n","MERGE_SORT(arr)\n","    if length(arr) > 1\n","        mid = length(arr) / 2\n","        left = arr[0 to mid-1]\n","        right = arr[mid to end]\n","\n","        MERGE_SORT(left)\n","        MERGE_SORT(right)\n","\n","        MERGE(arr, left, right)\n","\n","--------------------------------------\n","\n","MERGE(arr, left, right)\n","    i = j = k = 0\n","\n","    while i < length(left) and j < length(right)\n","        if left[i] <= right[j]\n","            arr[k] = left[i]\n","            i = i + 1\n","        else\n","            arr[k] = right[j]\n","            j = j + 1\n","        k = k + 1\n","\n","    while i < length(left)\n","        arr[k] = left[i]\n","        i = i + 1\n","        k = k + 1\n","\n","    while j < length(right)\n","        arr[k] = right[j]\n","        j = j + 1\n","        k = k + 1\n","\n","\n","```\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"jhCC-YOaKDmB"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Example of Merge sort\n","\n","```\n","Given Array\n","[38, 27, 43, 3]\n","\n","Step 1: Divide the Array\n","\n","Split the array until each sub-array has one element.\n","\n","    [38, 27, 43, 3]\n","           ↓\n","[38, 27]      [43, 3]\n","     ↓            ↓\n","[38] [27]     [43] [3]\n","\n","Step 2: Merge & Sort Sub-arrays\n","Merge [38] and [27]\n","\n","Compare 38 and 27\n","\n","27 is smaller → place first\n","\n","[27, 38]\n","\n","Merge [43] and [3]\n","\n","Compare 43 and 3\n","\n","3 is smaller → place first\n","\n","[3, 43]\n","\n","Step 3: Final Merge\n","\n","Merge [27, 38] and [3, 43]\n","\n","Compare\tPick\tResult Array\n","27 vs 3\t3\t[3]\n","27 vs 43\t27\t[3, 27]\n","38 vs 43\t38\t[3, 27, 38]\n","Remaining\t43\t[3, 27, 38, 43]\n","\n","Final Sorted Array\n","[3, 27, 38, 43]"],"metadata":{"id":"AgMA6hqnKDmB"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Quick sort"],"metadata":{"id":"FO5_VBnaXmh3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Quick Sort is a divide and conquer sorting algorithm.\n","It selects a pivot element, places it at the correct position, and rearranges elements so that:\n","\n","- Elements smaller than pivot are on the left\n","- Elements greater than pivot are on the right\n","\n","Then the same process is applied recursively to left and right sub-arrays.\n","\n","\n","- Very fast in practice\n","- In-place sorting algorithm\n","- Uses recursion\n","- Not a stable sort\n","\n","\n","```\n","Time Complexity:\n","Best Case: O(n log n)\n","Average Case: O(n log n)\n","Worst Case: O(n²) (when pivot is smallest or largest)\n","\n","Space Complexity: O(log n)\n","```\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"Hj1FimmHXmh4"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Algorithm Steps (Quick Sort)\n"],"metadata":{"id":"ftzjIWPCXmh4"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["Start\n","Choose a pivot element (first / last / middle)\n","Partition the array around the pivot\n","Place pivot at its correct position\n","Apply Quick Sort on left sub-array\n","Apply Quick Sort on right sub-array\n","Stop"],"metadata":{"id":"HjDLQqrRXmh4"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","#### Pseudocode (quick Sort)\n","\n","```\n","QUICK_SORT(arr, low, high)\n","    if low < high\n","        p = PARTITION(arr, low, high)\n","\n","        QUICK_SORT(arr, low, p - 1)\n","        QUICK_SORT(arr, p + 1, high)\n","\n","\n","--------------------------------------\n","\n","PARTITION(arr, low, high)\n","    pivot = arr[high]\n","    i = low - 1\n","\n","    for j = low to high - 1\n","        if arr[j] < pivot\n","            i = i + 1\n","            swap arr[i] and arr[j]\n","\n","    swap arr[i + 1] and arr[high]\n","    return i + 1\n","\n","\n","\n","```\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"BFhGklv1Xmh5"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Example of quick sort\n","\n","```\n","Given Array\n","[10, 7, 8, 9, 1, 5]\n","\n","Pivot = last element\n","\n","Step 1: First Partition (Pivot = 5)\n","Compare 10 with 5 → no swap\n","Compare 7 with 5 → no swap\n","Compare 8 with 5 → no swap\n","Compare 9 with 5 → no swap\n","Compare 1 with 5 → swap 1 and 10\n","\n","Array becomes:\n","\n","[1, 7, 8, 9, 10, 5]\n","\n","\n","Now swap pivot (5) with 7:\n","\n","[1, 5, 8, 9, 10, 7]\n","\n","\n","Pivot 5 is now at correct position.\n","\n","Step 2: Left Sub-array\n","Left of pivot:\n","[1]\n","\n","Single element → already sorted.\n","\n","Step 3: Right Sub-array (Pivot = 7)\n","Sub-array:\n","[8, 9, 10, 7]\n","\n","Compare 8 with 7 → no swap\n","Compare 9 with 7 → no swap\n","Compare 10 with 7 → no swap\n","\n","Swap pivot (7) with 8:\n","\n","[7, 9, 10, 8]\n","\n","Step 4: Continue Sorting Right Side\n","Sub-array:\n","[9, 10, 8]\n","Pivot = 8\n","\n","Compare 9 and 10 → no swaps\n","\n","Swap pivot with 9:\n","\n","[8, 10, 9]\n","\n","Step 5: Final Small Partition\n","Sub-array:\n","[10, 9]\n","Pivot = 9\n","\n","Swap 9 and 10:\n","[9, 10]\n","\n","Final Sorted Array\n","[1, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10]"],"metadata":{"id":"hdUZ9sYOXmh5"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Searching"],"metadata":{"id":"BeO1eJHexClo"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"psiLIKe-THK6"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Linear search:\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"z7dnRk0gTMlU"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Linear Search** is the simplest searching technique where each element of the list is checked one by one until the required element is found or the list ends.\n","\n","- Also called Sequential Search\n","- Works on sorted and unsorted data\n","- Checks elements from start to end\n","- Easy to understand and implement\n","\n","\n","```\n","Time Complexity\n","Best Case: O(1) (element found at first position)\n","Average Case: O(n)\n","Worst Case: O(n) (element not found or at last position)\n","\n","Space Complexity\n","O(1)\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"HQ-Vua_WTMlV"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Algorithm Steps (Linear Search)\n","\n","```\n","Step 1: Start\n","Step 2: Read array A and element X to search\n","Step 3: Set index i = 0\n","Step 4: Compare A[i] with X\n","Step 5:\n","    If A[i] == X, display Element found at index i and Stop\n","    Else increment i by 1\n","Step 6: Repeat Steps 4–5 until i < n\n","Step 7: If element is not found, display Element not found\n","Step 8: Stop\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"NCdp05M9Txqc"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Pseudocode (Linear Search)\n","\n","```\n","LinearSearch(A, X):\n","    for i ← 0 to length(A) - 1 do\n","        if A[i] == X then\n","            return i\n","    return -1   // Element not found\n","\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"enyWY8-xTxqd"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Example of linear Search\n","\n","```\n","Array: A = [15, 22, 9, 31, 42, 7]\n","\n","Element to search: X = 31\n","\n","\n","Step 1: Compare A[0] = 15 with 31\n","→ Not equal, move to next element\n","\n","Step 2: Compare A[1] = 22 with 31\n","→ Not equal, move to next element\n","\n","Step 3: Compare A[2] = 9 with 31\n","→ Not equal, move to next element\n","\n","Step 4: Compare A[3] = 31 with 31\n","→ Match found\n","\n","Element 31 is found at index 3\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"3FvL7aoRUET5"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Binary search:\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"zPdeohFLxGco"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Binary Search** is an efficient searching algorithm used to find an element in a sorted array by repeatedly dividing the search interval into two halves.\n","\n","- Works only on sorted data\n","- Follows divide and conquer approach\n","- Compares the middle element with the target value\n","- Reduces search range by half in each step\n","\n","\n","```\n","Time Complexity\n","\n","Best Case: O(1)\n","Average Case: O(log n)\n","Worst Case: O(log n)\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"oCe7ZqyrRo2U"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Algorithm Steps (Binary Search)\n","\n","```\n","Step 1: Start\n","Step 2: Take a sorted array A, target value X\n","Step 3: Set low = 0 and high = n - 1\n","Step 4: While low ≤ high, do the following:\n","    a. Compute mid = (low + high)\n","    b. If A[mid] == X, display Element found at index mid and Stop\n","    c. If A[mid] < X, set low = mid + 1\n","    d. Else set high = mid - 1\n","Step 5: If the loop ends, display Element not found\n","Step 6: Stop\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"nSajaeskSJgK"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Pseudocode (Binary Search)\n","\n","```\n","BinarySearch(A, X):\n","    low ← 0\n","    high ← length(A) - 1\n","\n","    while low ≤ high do\n","        mid ← (low + high)\n","\n","        if A[mid] == X then\n","            return mid\n","        else if A[mid] < X then\n","            low ← mid + 1\n","        else\n","            high ← mid - 1\n","\n","    return -1   // Element not found\n","\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"kPHbakMJR6D2"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Binary Search Example\n","\n","```\n","Sorted Array:\n","A = [4, 7, 10, 14, 19, 27, 32, 42]\n","\n","Element to search:\n","X = 19\n","\n","Step 1:\n","low = 0, high = 7\n","mid = (0 + 7)\n","Compare A[3] = 14 with 19\n","→ 14 < 19, search right half\n","Set low = 4\n","\n","Step 2:\n","low = 4, high = 7\n","mid = (4 + 7)\n","Compare A[5] = 27 with 19\n","→ 27 > 19, search left half\n","Set high = 4\n","\n","Step 3:\n","low = 4, high = 4\n","mid = (4 + 4)\n","Compare A[4] = 19 with 19\n","→ Match found\n","\n","✅ Result\n","\n","Element 19 is found at index 4\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"JZlkq0f7U_b8"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Binary Search Example 2\n","\n","```\n","Step 1\n","Low = 0\n","High = 19\n","Mid = (0 + 19) // 2 = 9\n","Mid Element = Kavya\n","\n","Comparison:\n","\n","\"Meena\" > \"Kavya\"\n","➡ Search in right half\n","\n","Step 2\n","Low = 10\n","High = 19\n","Mid = (10 + 19) // 2 = 14\n","\n","Mid Element = Praveen\n","\n","Comparison:\n","\n","\"Meena\" < \"Praveen\"\n","➡ Search in left half\n","\n","Step 3\n","Low = 10\n","High = 13\n","Mid = (10 + 13) // 2 = 11\n","\n","Mid Element = Manoj\n","\n","Comparison:\n","\"Meena\" > \"Manoj\"\n","➡ Search in right half\n","\n","Step 4\n","Low = 12\n","High = 13\n","Mid = (12 + 13) // 2 = 12\n","\n","Mid Element = Meena\n","\n","Comparison:\n","\n","\"Meena\" == \"Meena\"\n","Element Found\n","Result\n","Meena is found at index 12\n","```"],"metadata":{"id":"adx-kUGEaknq"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Trees\n"],"metadata":{"id":"3kDIw2oK3qJZ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Binary Search Tree"],"metadata":{"id":"QoLOZXmG3uxb"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["A Binary Search Tree (BST) is a special type of binary tree in which:\n","\n","- Each node has at most two children (left and right)\n","\n","- Left subtree contains values less than the node\n","\n","- Right subtree contains values greater than the node\n","\n","- No duplicate values (in standard BST)\n","\n","\n","\n","> A Binary Search Tree is a binary tree where the left subtree contains smaller elements and the right subtree contains larger elements than the root. It allows efficient searching, insertion, and deletion operations.\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"VijpYvU384S0"}}]}